  "id": "stereotype-threat",
  "term": "stereotype threat",
  "definition": "Stereotype threat is a psychology concept describing how people from a group that is viewed negatively may do worse on academic or thinking tasks because the stereotype itself has harmful effects. It is often discussed as a possible factor in group differences in advanced education and STEM participation, although the strength of the evidence has been debated.",
